<title>UK: JWT wins $6.9 mln Hamburg-Mannheimer ad account.</title>
<headline>JWT wins $6.9 mln Hamburg-Mannheimer ad account.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>J.Walter Thompson said on Wednesday its agency in Germany had won the $6.9 million account for Hamburg-Mannheimer Versicherungs AG, a German insurance group.</p>
<p>JWT said it won the account after tough competition against the incumbent agency, FCB Hamburg, Wilkens, and Baader Lang Behnken.</p>
<p>&quot;The agency won the business on the strength of its creative concept and integrated communications,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>JWT, a part of WPP Group Plc, will start working in early 1997 on the campaign, which will use &quot;Mr Kaiser&quot;, a well-known character in German advertising.</p>
<p>-- London Advertising Newsdesk +44 171 542 2792</p>
